+	<!-- custom: When enabled, city-assault armies at war with a rival whose spaceship has launched treat its reachable capital as an emergency objective instead of comparing it with ordinary conquest value. Capturing or razing the current capital during the active countdown resets the spaceship projects and stops the imminent victory; before launch, completed projects survive capital relocation, so ordinary target scoring remains in charge. A group only overrides its target when its path can arrive within the remaining countdown, then moves directly instead of spending that countdown on ordinary regrouping, healing retreats, opportunistic combat, reinforcement waits or upgrade waits. An army below its immediate attack threshold holds as soon as it is within one path turn to recover and receive reinforcements, avoiding exposure beside the city when possible; it advances and forces its assault only when no countdown slack remains. Base AdvCiv's existing enough-offence-en-route check can leave surplus armies available for other targets. See KI#190. (GPT-5.6-Sol) -->
+	<Define>
+		<DefineName>SAS_AI_SPACE_VICTORY_DENIAL_CAPITAL_RUSH_ENABLE</DefineName>
+		<iDefineIntVal>1</iDefineIntVal>
+	</Define>

